    "id": "MERGE-INPUT-ALIASING",
    "report": "A36",
    "note": "The baseline copies only what the update contributes, so a subtree the base alone provides stays the very same object inside the result. SPEC.md amendment 7 requires a merge that does not mutate its inputs, and an aliasing result mutates them indirectly: writing through the result writes through the base document that a caller is still reading. The corrected result is a fresh tree throughout."
